<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Kraken ID Parse report — {{ report.sample_id }}</title>
  <style>
    /* Shared visual language with the rest of the Kapur Lab suite (amr_plus,
       irma): teal/terra/ink, one flowing document with underlined section
       headings, label/value tables for facts and grid tables for rows. The
       report used to imitate a paginated LaTeX document — a date stamp
       repeated on every "page" and dark blue title bars — which read as a
       printout of something else rather than as this tool's own output. */
    :root {
      --ink: #1F2A2E;
      --muted: #6E7B82;
      --teal: #4C8C8A;
      --teal-dark: #2F6F6C;
      --terra: #C88F7A;
      --border: #E3DED6;
      --panel: #FBFAF8;
      --stripe: #F6F5F2;
      --danger: #C46A6A;
      --success: #6BAA75;
      --warn: #D8B26E;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      color: var(--ink);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 24px;
      max-width: 1100px;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.45;
      background: #fff;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 2px; }
    h2 {
      color: var(--teal);
      font-size: 15px;
      margin: 22px 0 6px;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
      padding-bottom: 3px;
    }
    h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 4px; }
    .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 12px; }
    .banner {
      background: var(--teal);
      color: #fff;
      padding: 10px 14px;
      border-radius: 6px;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin: 6px 0;
    }
    .banner.danger { background: var(--danger); }
    .banner.warn { background: var(--warn); }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 4px 0 8px; }
    table.kv th {
      text-align: left;
      width: 34%;
      background: var(--panel);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    table.kv th, table.kv td {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 5px 9px;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    table.grid { font-size: 11.5px; }
    table.grid th {
      background: var(--teal);
      color: #fff;
      text-align: left;
      padding: 5px 7px;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    table.grid td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 4px 7px; }
    table.grid tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: var(--stripe); }
    td.numeric, th.numeric { text-align: right; }
    .nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
    td.center, th.center { text-align: center; }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); }
    .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; }
    .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
    .figure { margin: 8px 0 10px; }
    .figure img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
    .pie { max-width: 460px; }
    .caption { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; margin: 2px 0 12px; }
    .chips span {
      display: inline-block;
      background: #EEF3F2;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 1px 9px;
      margin: 2px 3px 0 0;
      font-size: 11px;
    }
    a { color: var(--teal-dark); }
    @page { size: letter; margin: 14mm; }
    @media print {
      body { padding: 0; font-size: 11px; max-width: none; }
      h2 { break-after: avoid; }
      table, .figure { break-inside: avoid; }
      .no-print { display: none; }
      /* Plotly cannot render in a print engine; the static coverage figures
         below carry the same information into the PDF. */
      .coverage-interactive { display: none; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
{% set legacy = report.legacy_report %}
{% set blast_name = (report.parameters.blast_db or "BLAST database").split("/")[-1] %}
{% set target_taxon = legacy.target.taxon or report.parameters.taxon %}

<h1>Kraken ID Parse — read classification &amp; identification report</h1>
<p class="sub">
  Sample <b>{{ report.sample_id }}</b> &middot; {{ report.report_date }}
  {%- if report.software and report.software.pipeline_git_commit %} &middot; pipeline {{ report.software.pipeline_git_commit }}{% endif %}
</p>

{% if report.status and report.status != "completed" %}
  <div class="banner warn">Run status: {{ report.status.replace("_", " ") }} — see the warnings at the end of this report.</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="banner">
  {%- if target_taxon %}Target taxon: {{ target_taxon }}{% else %}Taxonomic classification{% endif %}
  {%- if legacy.target.extraction_rate %} &middot; {{ legacy.target.extraction_rate|fmt(2, "%") }} of reads extracted{% endif %}
  {%- if legacy.assembly.contig_count %} &middot; {{ legacy.assembly.contig_count }} contigs assembled{% endif %}
</div>

<h2>What this report shows</h2>
<p>
  Every read in this sample was classified against a Kraken2 database to identify what
  organisms are present and to screen for contamination.
  {%- if target_taxon %}
  Reads assigned to <b>{{ target_taxon }}</b> were then extracted
  {%- if legacy.target.extracted_reads %} ({{ legacy.target.extracted_reads|fmt }} of
  {{ legacy.target.total_input_reads|fmt }} reads){% endif %}
  {%- if legacy.assembly.contig_count %}, assembled, and the assembly identified by BLAST
  against {{ blast_name }}{% endif %}.
  {%- endif %}
  Each section below reports one step, with the numbers it produced.
</p>

<h2>Input file quality</h2>
<p class="small">
  Read statistics per FASTQ file. Q30 is the percentage of bases at or above Phred quality
  30 (a 1-in-1000 error rate); higher is better.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
  <table class="grid">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>File</th><th class="numeric">Size</th><th class="numeric">Q30 passing</th>
        <th class="numeric">Mean read score</th><th class="numeric">Average read length</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in legacy.fastq if row.filename %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.filename }}</td>
        <td class="numeric">{{ row.file_size }}</td>
        <td class="numeric">{{ row.q30 }}</td>
        <td class="numeric">{{ row.mean_score|fmt(1) }}</td>
        <td class="numeric">{{ row.avg_length|fmt(1) }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

{% if report.artifacts | selectattr("name", "equalto", "bracken_pie.png") | list %}
  <h2>Read identification</h2>
  <div class="figure">
    <img class="pie" src="{{ asset_url("bracken_pie.png") }}" alt="FASTQ read identification pie chart">
  </div>
  <p class="caption">
    Share of reads assigned to each organism, from
    <a href="https://ccb.jhu.edu/software/kraken2/">Kraken2</a> classification re-estimated by
    <a href="https://ccb.jhu.edu/software/bracken/">Bracken</a>.
  </p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Kraken classification</h2>
<table class="kv">
  <tbody>
    <tr><th>Target taxon</th><td>{{ target_taxon or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Taxon ID</th><td>{{ legacy.target.taxon_id or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Total input reads</th><td>{{ legacy.target.total_input_reads|fmt }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Extracted reads</th><td>{{ legacy.target.extracted_reads|fmt }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Extraction rate</th><td>{{ legacy.target.extraction_rate|fmt(2, "%") }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Kraken2 database</th><td>{{ (report.parameters.kraken_db or "not recorded").split("/")[-1] }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

{% if legacy.target_taxonomy %}
  <h2>Detailed classification</h2>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table class="grid">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Taxonomic name</th><th class="center">Level</th><th class="numeric">Reads</th><th class="numeric">Percent</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for row in legacy.target_taxonomy %}
        <tr>
          <td>{{ row.name }}</td>
          <td class="center">{{ row.level }}</td>
          <td class="numeric">{{ row.reads|fmt }}</td>
          <td class="numeric">{{ row.percent|fmt(2) }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="caption">Reads assigned at each rank in the target lineage. Level codes follow Kraken2: G genus, S species, and numbered sub-ranks below them.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if legacy.assembly.contig_count or legacy.assembly.total_length %}
  <h2>Assembly</h2>
  <table class="kv">
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Contig count</th><td>{{ legacy.assembly.contig_count or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Contig length counts (&lt;300 | 301–999 | &gt;999 bp)</th><td>{{ legacy.assembly.contig_bins or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Longest contig</th><td>{{ legacy.assembly.longest_contig|fmt }} bp</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Total length</th><td>{{ legacy.assembly.total_length|fmt }} bp</td></tr>
      <tr><th>N50</th><td>{{ legacy.assembly.n50|fmt }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Mean coverage (from FASTQ)</th><td>{{ legacy.assembly.mean_coverage or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="caption">N50 is the contig length at which half the assembly sits in contigs that long or longer — a standard summary of assembly contiguity.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Assembly identification — BLAST against {{ blast_name }}</h2>
{% if legacy.blast_rows %}
  <div class="scroll">
    <table class="grid">
      <thead><tr><th class="numeric nowrap">Bases (nt)</th><th class="numeric nowrap">Contigs</th><th>Best-matching subject</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {# Strongest match FIRST. The summary file is written weakest-to-strongest
         (the pipeline reads its LAST line to pick the reference), so printing it
         in file order buries the identification at the bottom of the table. #}
      {% for row in legacy.blast_rows|reverse %}
        <tr>
          <td class="numeric">{{ row.nt_base_count|fmt }}</td>
          <td class="numeric">{{ row.contigs }}</td>
          <td>{{ row.description }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="caption">
    Assembled contigs grouped by the reference they matched best, strongest first: the top row
    carries the most assembled sequence and is the identification this run supports.
  </p>
{% else %}
  <p class="muted">No BLAST summary rows were found for this run.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if legacy.coverage_interactive %}
  <h2>Coverage &amp; variants</h2>
  <p class="small">
    Per-position read depth for each reference, with a diamond at every variant position and,
    beneath each diamond, a stem coloured by the nucleotides actually observed there in
    proportion (A green, C blue, G yellow, T red) — so a 50/50 G/A call is a stem that is half
    yellow, half green. Shaded red spans have no coverage; the dashed line is 100X.
    <span class="no-print">Drag to zoom into any region; double-click resets.</span>
  </p>
  <div class="coverage-interactive">{{ legacy.coverage_interactive|safe }}</div>
{% endif %}

{% for figure in legacy.coverage_figures %}
  {% if loop.first %}<h2>Coverage analysis</h2>{% endif %}
  {% if figure.preview_path %}
    <div class="figure">
      <img src="{{ asset_url(figure.preview_path) }}" alt="Coverage depth analysis">
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Figure {{ loop.index }}: read depth across the reference sequences the assembly was compared against.</p>
  {% else %}
    <p class="muted">Coverage graph: {{ figure.path }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if loop.last and legacy.coverage_stats %}
    <div class="scroll">
      <table class="grid">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Reference</th><th class="numeric">Length</th><th class="numeric">Mean coverage</th><th class="numeric">Genome covered</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for row in legacy.coverage_stats %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ row.header }}</td>
            <td class="numeric">{{ row.length|fmt }}</td>
            <td class="numeric">{{ row.mean_coverage|fmt(1, "X") }}</td>
            <td class="numeric">{{ row.percent_covered|fmt(1, "%") }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Alignment statistics for each reference sequence.</p>
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<h2>Methods &amp; provenance</h2>
<table class="kv">
  <tbody>
    <tr><th>Kraken2 database</th><td>{{ report.parameters.kraken_db or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>BLAST database</th><td>{{ report.parameters.blast_db or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
    {% if report.software %}
      {% if report.software.bracken %}<tr><th>Bracken</th><td>{{ report.software.bracken }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
      {% if report.software.blastn %}<tr><th>BLAST</th><td>{{ report.software.blastn }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
      {% if report.software.python %}<tr><th>Python</th><td>{{ report.software.python }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
      {% if report.software.pipeline_git_commit %}<tr><th>Pipeline revision</th><td>{{ report.software.pipeline_git_commit }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if report.environment and report.environment.hostname %}<tr><th>Host</th><td>{{ report.environment.hostname }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    <tr><th>Run identifier</th><td>{{ report.run_id or "not recorded" }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="small">
  Disclaimer: taxonomic assignment and BLAST identification are genotypic predictions made
  against reference databases, and depend on what those databases contain — an organism absent
  from the database cannot be reported. Low extraction rates, fragmented assemblies and thin
  coverage all weaken an identification. These results support, but do not replace,
  confirmatory testing. The complete output file set, including
  <code>run_manifest.json</code> with the full machine-readable record of this run, is
  available from the tool's Results pane.
</p>

{% if report.warnings %}
  <h2>Warnings</h2>
  <ul class="small">
  {% for warning in report.warnings %}
    <li>{{ warning }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endif %}

</body>
</html>
